  "method": "belief-information",
  "outcome": "Update a belief and calculate gross and net one-step information value.",
  "prerequisites": [
    "Python lists and dictionaries",
    "The mapped chapter and its notation"
  ],
  "routes": [
    "Bayesian hidden-state belief update",
    "one-step value of observation",
    "uninformative signal aliasing"
  ],
  "input_fields": {
    "belief": "Normalized prior state probability list.",
    "transition": "Square row-stochastic state transition matrix.",
    "observation": "State by observation row-stochastic matrix.",
    "observed": "Zero-based observation index.",
    "action_rewards": "Action by state finite reward matrix.",
    "observation_cost": "Nonnegative cost paid before the one later action."
  },
  "example_input": "data/examples/ch08.json",
  "reader": "readers/08-belief-information/reader.html",
  "equations": [
    {
      "label": "EQV8-01",
      "number": "8.1",
      "tex": "\\mathbf{b}_{t+1}(x') \\;=\\;\n\\frac{\\begin{gathered}\n\\operatorname{Obs}(o\\mid x',a)\\\\\n\\cdot\\sum_{x\\in\\mathcal{X}}P(x'\\mid x,a)\\,\\mathbf{b}_t(x)\n\\end{gathered}}\n{\\begin{gathered}\n\\sum_{x''\\in\\mathcal{X}}\\operatorname{Obs}(o\\mid x'',a)\\\\\n\\cdot\\sum_{x\\in\\mathcal{X}}P(x''\\mid x,a)\\,\\mathbf{b}_t(x)\n\\end{gathered}}.\n\\tag{8.1}",
      "asset": "assets/math/e992bac4f67c2b9f4efc.svg",
      "explanations": [
        "Equation (8.1) turns yesterday's belief, one action, and one observation into today's belief.",
        "Push the old belief forward through the action, weight each destination by how well it explains what was seen, then rescale so the weights sum to one."
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "chapter-08-display-2",
      "number": "un-numbered display 2",
      "tex": "T_E=\\begin{pmatrix}\n0.1&0.9&0&0\\\\\n0.1&0&0.9&0\\\\\n0&0.1&0&0.9\\\\\n0&0&0.1&0.9\n\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad\n\\operatorname{Obs}(\\text{non-goal}\\mid x')=(1,1,0,1).",
      "asset": "assets/math/aeaa392b80c6a5400cb4.svg",
      "explanations": []
    },
    {
      "label": "EQV8-02",
      "number": "8.2",
      "tex": "\\bar r(\\mathbf{b},a)\\;=\\;\\sum_{x\\in\\mathcal{X}}\\mathbf{b}(x)\\,r(x,a).\n\\tag{8.2}",
      "asset": "assets/math/c2b31b3a9ae02b649313.svg",
      "explanations": [
        "Equation (8.2) prices an action under uncertainty about where the agent is.",
        "Average the reward the action would earn in each state, weighting each state by how much belief sits on it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "EQV8-03",
      "number": "8.3",
      "tex": "\\begin{aligned}\nV(\\mathbf{b})\n&=\\max_{a\\in\\mathcal{A}}\\Big[\\,\\bar r(\\mathbf{b},a)\\\\\n&\\quad+\\gamma\\sum_{o}\\Pr(o\\mid \\mathbf{b},a)\\,\nV\\big(\\mathbf{b}'(\\mathbf{b},a,o)\\big)\\Big].\n\\end{aligned}\n\\tag{8.3}",
      "asset": "assets/math/cd4610a982670be0201e.svg",
      "explanations": [
        "Equation (8.3) values a belief by the best action available from it and the beliefs that action can lead to.",
        "Take the immediate expected reward, add the discounted average value of the belief each possible observation would produce, and keep the best action."
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "chapter-08-display-5",
      "number": "8.4",
      "tex": "V_H(\\mathbf b)=\\max_{\\alpha\\in\\Gamma_H}\\alpha^\\top\\mathbf b.\n\\tag{8.4}",
      "asset": "assets/math/a29d857519b0a313b7c7.svg",
      "explanations": [
        "Equation (8.4) represents finite-horizon belief value as best dot product from finite policy-vector set.",
        "Score each contingent plan against current belief, then select largest expected return."
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "EQV8-04",
      "number": "8.5",
      "tex": "\\begin{aligned}\n\\operatorname{VOI}(O)\n&=\\sum_{o}\\Pr(o\\mid\\mathbf{b})\\,\n\\max_{a\\in\\mathcal{A}}\\bar r\\big(\\mathbf{b}'(\\mathbf{b},o),a\\big)\\\\\n&\\quad-\\max_{a\\in\\mathcal{A}}\\bar r(\\mathbf{b},a).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\tag{8.5}",
      "asset": "assets/math/56c0b286f79d620e6ec3.svg",
      "explanations": [
        "Equation (8.5) prices a look by how much better the decision becomes once its answer is known.",
        "Average the best achievable reward across the beliefs each possible answer would leave, then subtract the best achievable reward without looking."
      ]
    }
  ],
